==English==
[[File:Ganesh in legno di sandalo.jpg|thumb|right|A statue of Ganesha]]

===Alternative forms===
* [[Ganesa]]
* [[Ganesh]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sa}} {{term|sc=Deva|गणेश|tr=Gaṇeśa|lang=sa}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{Hinduism}} A [[Hindu]] [[god]] of [[intellect]], [[wisdom]], [[gate]]s{{,}} and [[beginning]]s, son of [[Parvati]] and [[Shiva]].
# {{given name|male|from=Sanskrit}} used in India.

====Synonyms====
* [[Aumkara]], [[Ekadanta]], [[Gajanana]], [[Ganapati]], [[Lambodara]], [[Shurpa Karna]], [[Umaputra]], [[Vakratunda]], [[Vighnaharta]], [[Vinayaka]]

